{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>My people — its oppressors [are] a child.</b> Each one of its oppressors is a child, and the mem is added, and it is a noun adjective, not a verb." "Alef in <b>מאשריך</b> in place of yod, for the letters yod, he, vav, alef interchange, like אשרו חמוץ (Isaiah 1:17), and the meaning: those who would straighten your path, they make it crooked." "<b>They have swallowed.</b> They have ruined, until the way is unknown."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:43.479155385Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}